  "body": "Removes the policy-controlled \"document-domain\" feature. This feature was specified for the benefit of Permissions and Document Policy. If the feature was enabled, assigment to document.domain was aborted with a SecurityException.\n\nThe feature-controlled assignment to document.domain was implemented in Chromium browsers, but never default enabled. The originally intended goal of this feature is now being served by the Origin-Agent-Cluster http header.\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * According to MDN and caniuse, only Chromium-based browsers have implemented Document Policy and Feature Policy. Thus other browsers probably haven't implemented any specific policy-controlled features, either.\n   * Chromium will remove Feature and Document Policies for document.domain here: https://crrev.com/c/3930823\n- [ ] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * WPT tests are being updated here: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/37036\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: n/a (https://crrev.com/c/3930823)\n   * Gecko: n/a (feature has not been implemented)\n   * WebKit: n/a (feature has not been implemented)\n   * Deno (only for timers, structured clone, base64 utils, channel messaging, module resolution, web workers, and web storage): n/a\n   * Node.js (only for timers, structured clone, base64 utils, channel messaging, and module resolution): n/a\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: n/a\n  * https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/22732\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/8549/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Dec 5, 2022, 4:46 AM UTC (414f174)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/8549/77d52c7...414f174/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Dec 5, 2022, 4:46 AM UTC (414f174)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/8549/browsers.html\" title=\"Last updated on Dec 5, 2022, 4:46 AM UTC (414f174)\">/browsers.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/8549/77d52c7...414f174/browsers.html\" title=\"Last updated on Dec 5, 2022, 4:46 AM UTC (414f174)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/8549/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Dec 5, 2022, 4:46 AM UTC (414f174)\">/infrastructure.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/8549/77d52c7...414f174/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Dec 5, 2022, 4:46 AM UTC (414f174)\">diff</a> )",
